          "explanation": "The 'virgin land' narrative imagined a near-empty wilderness awaiting settlers. Mann, Crosby, William Denevan, and a generation of ethnohistorians and archaeologists have shown the opposite: tens of millions of people, sophisticated polities (Cahokia, Tenochtitlan, the Haudenosaunee), and a catastrophic collapse — perhaps 90% — driven primarily by Old World pathogens. This reframing is foundational to modern US history pedagogy.",
